{"kind":"artifact","text":"The layer contract names the platform it was exercised on, and the trust scope it actually has. Exact clean pushed head 5bc84ca2f3dbfd57258450ce76f32ed7c37b6922 on request/repo-remote-link; tree 24f3ee86, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's round-six child f42f5e35 and my promise 8bdb5b67.\n\nTHREE CLAIMS OF MINE WERE WRONG AND ARE REPLACED.\n\nThe environment claim now says what it can. On Unix, which is where this is exercised, the stated set is the whole of the child's environment. Windows is named as a second boundary this layer does not state — the package builds for it, nothing has been run on it, and the property is false there because Go's os/exec appends SYSTEMROOT from the parent whenever the child environment carries no name folding to it. That is outside the contract rather than a caveat inside it, which is planner's ruling and is the same rule this lane keeps relearning applied one level up: a boundary claim must name the platform it was demonstrated on.\n\nThe scope claim now names local configuration, worktree configuration where extensions.worktreeConfig is set, and include and includeIf targets absolute or relative — each measured to execute core.fsmonitor during an ordinary status read. I had written 'the repository's own configuration file', which was the one case I had exercised.\n\nAnd PATH is gone from the description because it is gone from the code; the parent's binary selection is recorded as a deployment trust boundary this layer does not close.\n\nWHAT STAYS A PROPERTY. The citation guard, per the earlier ruling: it refuses whenever it cannot positively confirm that no live document cites the target, and no enumeration of variables, admitted or denied, is load-bearing. That wording was widened from 'no list of variable names' precisely because an allowlist is an enumeration too, and this head is what made that distinction bite.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached. npm test 131 pass, 0 fail. gofmt empty; build, vet, GOOS=windows build of internal/app and diff-check all exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"5bc84ca2f3dbfd57258450ce76f32ed7c37b6922","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}